# Blackbox Global Rules — ECOWAS Parliament Monorepo

## Repository layout
- apps/admin/  — CRM (staff portal, invitation-only)
- apps/web/    — Public ECOWAS Parliament website
- supabase/    — Edge functions (Deno) + SQL migrations

No root-level package.json. All npm commands must run from inside apps/admin/ or apps/web/.

## Coding conventions
- TypeScript strict mode throughout — no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`
- React components use named exports, not default exports (exception: page-level route files)
- shadcn/ui for all UI primitives; Tailwind for layout and spacing
- TanStack Query for all server state; Redux Toolkit only for pure UI state
- Sonner (`useToast`) for all toast notifications — never `alert()`
- Zod for all runtime validation at system boundaries (forms, API responses)

## Naming patterns
- CRM module files: `<PascalCase>Module.tsx` in apps/admin/src/components/crm/modules/
- Edge functions: `supabase/functions/<kebab-case>/index.ts`
- Migrations: `supabase/migrations/YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_<snake_case_description>.sql`
- Translation keys: dot-notation namespaced by UI area (e.g. `crm.tasks.title`)

## Auth & security rules
- NEVER use the Supabase service role key on the client side
- Every new table must have RLS enabled and at least one policy before any frontend query is written
- RLS policy pattern: `has_role(auth.uid(), 'role_name'::app_role)`
- isSuperAdmin UI checks are display-only — always enforce the same check server-side in RLS or edge functions
- Edge functions must authenticate BEFORE any DB operation (anonClient.auth.getUser() first)

## i18n rules
- All user-facing strings must use the `t()` helper from `useI18n()`
- Every key added to en.ts must be added to fr.ts and pt.ts in the same commit
- Untranslated stubs use the prefix `[NEEDS_TRANSLATION]`

## Files agents must never modify
- supabase/migrations/ — existing migration files are immutable once committed
- apps/admin/src/integrations/supabase/types.ts — auto-generated, regenerate with CLI only
- apps/web/src/integrations/supabase/types.ts — same as above
- amplify.yml — deployment config, change only on explicit instruction
- Any .env or .env.local file
